bug_investigation_logs |bug_id, line_num, content|
    optional_return_into_scalar_fn_accepted_2026-11-26, 0, "2026-11-26 filed from jit_dict_f64_key_get_membership_aarch64_2026-11-26 (float_get returned the Option heap word through -> i64)."
    optional_return_into_scalar_fn_accepted_2026-11-26, 1, "2026-11-26 fixed on work/bug-optional-return-scalar-20261126. Seed: validate_declared_return_type rejects T? returned where a char/int/float/text is declared (bool excluded: its return slot already decodes truthiness, the pinned _json_bool shape), checked BEFORE hir_types_compatible because T? shares the shared-pointer representation that check admits as T; verdicts carry error[E1003] (LOWERING_TYPE_ERROR_TAG) plus the return line, and exec_core.rs jit_failure_must_propagate refuses the interpreter fallback for that tag, so simple run exits 1 with the error (owner decision; also covers the existing float->int return/param rule). Array .sort() is now typed as the receiver array; untyped, xs.sort().join() hit the by-name .join suffix search and typed as text?. Pure-Simple checker: Dict.get infers V? (u64 stays bare, as in the seed) and ?? (NullCoalesce) is inferred instead of failing as an unsupported expression kind. Blast radius: 5 lib functions in a 400-file sample, plus 3 nogc_async_mut twins found via check/main.spl, all fixed as real latent bugs (dir_prevention_env_value returned the Option on a cache hit). Enforced re-sweep of the 400 files: 0 E1003. check_optional_return_into_scalar_spec 1/4 -> 4/4."

